Z||000001||Sour Lemon||08-01-2001||01:25 AM||||I'd stay away from those IBM's.  The main reason is because it runs windows ce and I have had plenty of problems in the past with  wince crash and losing all my data.<BR>If you want a cheap notebook check on ebay.<BR>You should be able to pick up a IBM 560 for about $100.  Add another 40 for a new battery and you should be set.  The specs on the 560 are:<BR>Pentium 100-166(depends on the model)<BR>16-72 MBs of ram<BR>810-1.6 gig hd<BR>11.3 Dual Scan or 12.1 active matrix screen.<BR>(I recommend the active)<BR>External floppy.<BR>If you want to go up a little in price you can get a IBM 560x or 560z with a pentium 233<BR>for about 300.<BR>If you wanted to go a little higher than that <BR>I know a place that's selling used toshiba 3020ct's. <A HREF="http://www.hitechcafe.com/eshop/product.asp?dept%5Fid=14&sku=PORTEGE%2D3020CT" TARGET=_blank>http://www.hitechcafe.com/eshop/product.asp?dept%5Fid=14&sku=PORTEGE%2D3020CT</A> <P>I hope I helped a little.||||reg||13
